From 10b100cb1acdda778344a86b621b7ce5b90adccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NikoMalik <NikoMalik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:40:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: make the better_idle newidle cutoff actually
 apply

6.18.1-better_idle.patch added the avg_idle/2 check below the old one
instead of replacing it,so the two nested ifs only break when
avg_idle < cost,which is the upstream condition and the patch never
did anything

drop the old line so newidle balance stops once half of avg_idle is
used up by the domain costs,tasks get pulled less often on short idle
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 18204ff5b254..d7630e878159 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -15561,7 +15561,6 @@ static int sched_balance_newidle(struct rq *this_rq, struct rq_flags *rf)
 
 		update_next_balance(sd, &next_balance);
 
-		if (this_rq->avg_idle < curr_cost + sd->max_newidle_lb_cost)
 		if (this_rq->avg_idle/2 < curr_cost + sd->max_newidle_lb_cost)
 			break;
 
